From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Faust <willtechnoduck@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 16:08:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iOS: delay-load ARM64EC redirect; document why
 arm64x_check_call keeps the x18 read

import_dll redirects EC->EC imports from the x64 .hexpthk export thunk to the
ARM64-native target. The DELAY-LOAD path never did, so it stored the thunk:
measured fp = rpcrt4 base + 0x60800 with IsEcCode(fp)=0, i.e. NdrClientCall2's
FFS thunk. Apply the same redirect in LdrResolveDelayLoadedAPI, gated on the
importer being EC exactly as import_dll is. After the fix the same imports
resolve to native pool addresses with IsEcCode=1.

arm64x_check_call: the `ldr x16,[x18,#0x60]` PEB read is WRONG and is kept
anyway, now documented in place. iOS clobbers x18 (every SEGV dump shows
x18=0), so it fetches a garbage PEB and reports every target as non-EC.
Correcting it to the TSD-slot-275 path was A/B-proven to break CEF:
cef_log.txt went unwritten for 8 consecutive runs and returned the moment the
x18 read was restored, with run depth also going 20-24k -> 28929 unix calls.
Forcing everything through the x64 exit thunk is slow and breaks variadic
callees, but that detour also absorbs whatever EcCodeBitMap false positive the
correct version turns into a direct branch into x64 bytes run as ARM64.
Correct-but-unlandable until that false positive is found.

Also here: the probes that established the above ([ec-bind]/[ec-recheck]/
[ec-delay] in loader.c, [ctxh] + stack window in ndr_marshall.c,
[ndr-shift]/[ndr-param] in ndr_stubless.c, [unwind-trace] in signal_arm64ec.c).

(cherry picked from commit 82bee4545509fb50448e2b92db86baa5962d5143)
Madeira-commit: b003f3767603789a13b772936dbe3a928441dc17
Rebased: clean
Class: madeira-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-26-wine-latest-rebase.md
Offered-upstream: no
